Lillian Mae Gay Garrick (Born June 13, 1917 -                 

Lillie Mae Garrick 

Author- A Farmer's Daughter - "Life is Good but By No Means Easy"


The Dedication'''{{subst:add-on}}'''What did God do for me?.................'''

I remember all the hard times He has brought me through:

My first day of school (I was so afraid,but in my mind I knew everything was going to be all right.);  How hard my father and mother worked to take care of their family; when I was ten and sick with some kind of heart disease and terrible bouts of diarrhea; when I was twelve and sick again (this time it was Scarlet Fever, which was a deadly disease in those days.  I'll never forget the swelling of my body and the burning fever.  Through all of that I could hear my mother whispering many, many prayers.)  The pain and cramps I suffered throughout my teenage years; (God was with me.)  The death of my mother when I was only eighteen years old; (I was really hurt, but God was there.  My Father was a Mother and a Father for us from then on.)  The tornado I survived that tore our house into little shreds of wood that looked like kindling (Only God could have saved us.); my married life; raising and educating three children; building a  home and living to see our sons and daughters and our grand children.

God was good and wonderful to me.  It would take a book to tell all the things I've lived to see and do.  I want my children and grandchildren and great-grandchildren to know about my life and understand that life is good, but by no means easy.

At the time of this writing I am seventy one years old (born June 13, 1917) and I'm still enjoying the rewards of God's love.